WEBVTT

00:03:28.955 --> 00:03:33.000
My theory about what actually
compels us to watch sports.

00:03:33.793 --> 00:03:38.089
I spent seven years as a columnist
and feature writer at ESPN,

00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:42.301
and I did shows like "Around the Horn,"
"Outside the Lines," "First Take."

00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:45.221
And we would always look
at the sports calendar

00:03:45.263 --> 00:03:48.391
and try to pinpoint moments
when women's sports would be big --

00:03:48.432 --> 00:03:49.767
like, really big.

00:03:50.643 --> 00:03:53.229
And it was always the same two events,

00:03:53.271 --> 00:03:55.273
the Olympics, then the World Cup.

00:03:55.606 --> 00:03:56.857
Then, the Olympics.

00:03:56.857 --> 00:03:58.484
Toss some tennis in there,

00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:00.945
but mostly the Olympics and the World Cup.